{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230533Z","id":"f1d30bf1dcaa1dd369dd223ba7dd7dcfabeebc1672f99cc99287ffaefc9d6cdd","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.4 puts Search in the Mac toolbar, filtering the sidebar and, with Home selected, the grid. Toolbar.swift builds no NSSearchToolbarItem yet, so the filter (SidebarModel.filter) has its own field at the bottom of ClaxSidebar, which ⌘F focuses (SplitShell._showFilter); it narrows only the sidebar, not the grid.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"32a2bc85addd41327b0d0d70efaa35b5d5217bf7b5671a51138cb4b6a11463f2"},"summary":"The sidebar's filter is a field at the sidebar's foot, not the toolbar's NSSearchToolbarItem","tags":["macos","revisit:Toolbar.swift has an NSSearchToolbarItem","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar_model.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230575Z","id":"6998cc0534702ba09e6c6b6df890ec2817372d6d1904b5d60b7ab69bf8036147","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.2 asks for an unread-thread count as each row's trailing ClaxBadge. HomeHost keeps only the inbox's total (HomeHost.unread, from GET /api/inbox/summary); SidebarModel takes unreadOf for a per-app count, and apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart passes none, so every badge is hidden.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"204d6596e69d85eac8a7cd59f439a43b73edbbc8baec7381c882bfa2ec74b2a9"},"suggested_fix":"Count unread inbox items per artifact (a daemon summary by artifact, or HomeHost tallying inbox events) and pass it as SidebarModel.unreadOf.","summary":"App rows never show an unread count: nothing gives one per app","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230614Z","id":"8f99d57a0176c6fd6cc23f30bd2ff0fc2dd4939e2509632acb1eaa53c6fd9649","body":{"detail":"MacToolbar puts the sidebar toggle and the navigation group first and the window title after them, from the window's leading edge. With the sidebar 220 wide the title starts near x=172 and crosses the divider (seen in target/flutter-app/shots/split-app-mac-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_split_shots_test, where the toolbar is a stand-in drawn the same way). AppKit's split views keep the detail's items after the sidebar with NSTrackingSeparatorToolbarItem, which needs the sidebar's width on the native side.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"e30708215224dddb6121db900d355251412d574c9f34dc28035a6e1a47aa4474"},"suggested_fix":"Insert a tracking separator (or a fixed space sized from setSidebarWidth) in Toolbar.swift after the toggle, so Back, Forward and the title start at the detail.","summary":"The toolbar's toggle, Back, Forward and title sit right after the window buttons, over the sidebar: a long title runs across the sidebar's edge","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230907Z","id":"e77ade19dbf2be4e4ae508f74326de969fb9069cfdb26710805b3d9e7bb23fbc","body":{"detail":"SplitShell.fits gives the Material family the split from ClaxWidth.expanded; ClaxListPane is a ListTile list without Search or the rail, and at medium (600-839) Android pushes app routes as on a phone, since a single pane without the rail would leave no way back to Home. Plan Task 53 builds the rail and the medium form.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"973b31506b5aeff9b2136ceb28e919de30ab3d012a3771e1595a32a2b1611af0"},"summary":"The Material family splits only from expanded, with a plain list pane; at medium Android keeps the phone layout","tags":["android","split","revisit:the navigation rail lands (plan Task 53)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230946Z","id":"49debfa2d5cbb8de4d5fe60a9e9c02f610b6184f512408801c3a649277c540c4","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.2 asks for the system accent with focus and grey without. _SidebarTile uses Theme.colorScheme.primary; no channel reports NSColor.controlAccentColor yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":470},"end":{"line":480},"content_hash":"8abf2886c707d842e3c141b16e30cf13c045b1f0777a626a6b24cae3a6d50788"},"summary":"The selected row is filled with the theme's primary (agent green), not the Mac's system accent","tags":["macos","split","revisit:the Mac accent reaches Dart","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230975Z","id":"3a933ee7a968038c94fe95169ca38ca87eaf9cab5a173236af304b1d88554495","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:macos_app built, and the app ran from a scratch support directory (daemon on a free loopback port), but screencapture answered 'could not create image from window' for its window and for the display, so nothing was looked at. The renders of //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_split_shots_test draw stand-ins for the material, the window buttons and the toolbar.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"d2020308bc48942c8b16ee0ba33520c6df369602686fba2093a1e5697f7250ce"},"summary":"The split window is unverified in the running Mac app: the sidebar material through the clear view, the toolbar's toggle, the title and dragging the sidebar's edge","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:54:45.486182Z","id":"b2c766a6215f05e25786a2605a6fd3add9c60eab3d8a91c3bae385e0ad56104a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: SplitShell passes the sidebar's width to MacToolbar.setLeading(edge:), setItems sends {leading, edge}, and Toolbar.swift puts a SidebarEdgeView spacer after the leading items, sized so Back, Forward and the title start past the sidebar's edge. ToolbarTests 'testLeadingItemsOverASidebarAreFollowedByItsEdge' and 'testTheEdgeSpacerReachesTheSidebarsEdgeFromWhereItStarts', and mac_toolbar_test 'leading items over a sidebar send its width…' pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:macos_toolbar_test //apps/clax_app:ui_mac_mac_toolbar_test: PASSED). Its look in a running window is left with 4a5f7823 and 3a933ee7.","supersedes":"8f99d57a0176c6fd6cc23f30bd2ff0fc2dd4939e2509632acb1eaa53c6fd9649","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:54:45.735874Z","id":"38d3806108563fcdb7a4ba202587bab42fcb17e10696929cdd76c00579ec687b","body":{"detail":"SplitShell._report calls HomeHost.holdToolbar only when hasDesktopWindowChrome, because neither the Material list pane (lib/ui/split/list_pane.dart) nor the iPad has a place for New app, Inbox and Settings yet. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.3 gives the home app toolbar: true wherever the window's toolbar and the rail carry them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"0891eb82510430afeb756a2d0346cf316e93da961da665ff541435b6e1f3f75e"},"suggested_fix":"Hold the toolbar from the Material split once its rail carries New app (plan Task 53), and on the iPad once its toolbar does.","summary":"Only a Mac window's split holds the toolbar for the home app: on wide Android and the iPad the home app in the split keeps its own bar, search and New app beside the sidebar","tags":["split","revisit:when the rail or an iPad toolbar offers New app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:14:04.755620Z","id":"caf7f6c3cf2ef0c0d6a35773294a21ad7e24c53a8e65980a97b40b519c73c9eb","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.4 has one Search item that filters the sidebar, and the grid when Home is selected, on ⌘F. The sidebar keeps its own filter field (lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart, 'sidebar-filter') because an app's toolbar (lib/ui/app_screen.dart _toolbarItems) declares no Search item yet, so ⌘F with an app selected has nowhere else to go; with Home selected the toolbar's field is the grid's search, and the sidebar filter stays one ⌘F away once an app is selected. split_shell_test 'Command-F puts the keyboard in the toolbar's search with Home selected…' pins this.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":226},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"a0b444a9de7d259de2cbb15f52238fc654086ef55fc1fe795857300292fe8a00"},"summary":"⌘F goes to the toolbar's search only with Home selected; with an app selected it still opens the sidebar's filter, and the toolbar's search filters the grid, not the sidebar","tags":["split","macos","revisit:when an app's toolbar declares the Search item of §4.4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:19.715116Z","id":"05c0e170d282e0c5fca6a2d63c371d6f9f87b6198bc6229e5f602ed4eaf59851","body":{"detail":"MainMenu.xib has no Delete App or starred-app items, so AppKit never routes these keys to Dart while the page is first responder. Adding File › Delete App… (⌘⌫) and Window items for the starred apps (⌘1…⌘9) through MacMenu would make them work from the page as the other commands do; whether those items belong in the menu bar (§4.8 lists neither) is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":466},"end":{"line":474},"content_hash":"6f2f6ac2fbf4c1f128c64c7a444abca5d64e5e4758084c572db463006b25a373"},"summary":"⌘⌫, ⌘1…⌘9 and Space reach the shell only while a Flutter view has the keyboard: with an app's page (its WKWebView) focused they go to the page, and no menu item carries them","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:19.715179Z","id":"93f48ef646c17c1bc3c3f7d599020a0ae9402feeb507e0e19b95f8a1997435ad","body":{"detail":"In the split window the detail follows the selection (↑/↓ change both), so there is nothing further to open for an app. Moving focus into the detail is unverified with a page's WKWebView: Flutter's focus may land on the screen's first Flutter control rather than the page.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":235},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"515fc08575cf1e5f4df47d663ba0be3dd3a10cf92ffbc165f61927b58fe97a68"},"summary":"Space in the sidebar 'opens' the selected app by moving the keyboard into its detail (and a make's build view), since selecting a row already shows the app; a separate open state, or Space as Quick Look-style preview, was not taken","tags":["revisit:when the detail can hold an app that is selected but not yet loaded, or the page must take the keyboard on Space","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:19.715241Z","id":"fa27f61ad93aac79c88b0115f58d2a941ab58182a8d5b07ad0958db3a356575b","body":{"detail":"AppKit source lists show no hover fill at all; §4.10 asks for hover on rows. A translucent fg tint (as the unfocused selection uses, fg at 0.1) would sit on the material as AppKit's own fills do. Cosmetic; unverified over the real material.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":480},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"1cab0f1bc01da9d04b10b68a289883ab0dffca9619e36c06d2bedb8115f5b540"},"summary":"A hovered sidebar row is filled with the opaque hover token over the clear sidebar, so over the window's translucent sidebar material it reads as a solid warm block in dark (the split-hover-mac-dark render of apps/clax_app/test/ui/shots/split_shots_test.dart)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:22:31.603880Z","id":"94805e051bd2a5d55f2718c1fe4fdda1ba6caa1aa24b1595e1ab5d65cbfc077a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the focused selection is appleAccent, the system accent the window bridge reports; 'the system accent fills the selected sidebar row while the sidebar has the keyboard' passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_hover_test), and macos_window_bridge_test's testTheAccentIsAnsweredInEachAppearanceAndSentWhenItChanges passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:macos_window_bridge_test). Unverified in a running app: record 93117cae.","supersedes":"49debfa2d5cbb8de4d5fe60a9e9c02f610b6184f512408801c3a649277c540c4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.977627Z","id":"1038b7e03f1d3c2ea3226af1ade0dba48d0ea121d8e768d727865caece2c41aa","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3a933ee7a968038c94fe95169ca38ca87eaf9cab5a173236af304b1d88554495","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f1c07f346b12 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): the toolbar's Hide Sidebar, the title and subtitle and the sidebar beside the detail show in app-light.png and home-light.png. The sidebar material cannot be drawn from layers (the captures show the window's background colour there), and dragging the sidebar's edge is untested.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:06:48.464144Z","id":"5bd4c51824204ccba5ea226c90a6ea7c838ba724e706624abe1f3c4c2f5ccfc5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: SplitShell.fits now splits both families from ClaxWidth.medium, with the navigation rail and a Material list pane with Search; //apps/clax_app:ui_split_split_shell_test passes ('on Android at 1280 by 800 a rail of 80, a list pane of 360…', 'on Android at 700 the rail and one pane…')","supersedes":"e77ade19dbf2be4e4ae508f74326de969fb9069cfdb26710805b3d9e7bb23fbc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:06:48.512789Z","id":"f0899896d6c7cf4401a7e1a155c2add92f8754a04d8c91ddf9620400927f8516","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"38d3806108563fcdb7a4ba202587bab42fcb17e10696929cdd76c00579ec687b","summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 wide Android holds the toolbar at ClaxWidth.expanded (the rail carries New app, Inbox and Settings; the list pane's search sets HomeHost.setQuery), tested by 'wide Android holds the toolbar for the home app…' in test/ui/split/split_shell_test.dart. Still open: the iPad, and Android at medium (see the needs-decision record on SplitShellState._report).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:06:48.513661Z","id":"8d89d96004da2a15aedab1df15aad22068ea2e3ca380a987fa8b30f0f9c1e80e","body":{"detail":"SplitShellState._report holds HomeHost's toolbar for the Material family only at ClaxWidth.expanded, where ClaxListPane's search feeds HomeHost.setQuery. At medium no list pane shows, so holding would leave the grid without a search; not holding duplicates New app (and Inbox and Settings where the home app's bar has them). Options: (a) keep as is; (b) hold at medium too and put a search field above the grid in Flutter (or in the rail); (c) hold at medium and accept no search until Ctrl+F brings the list pane over the detail. Test: 'wide Android holds the toolbar…' in test/ui/split/split_shell_test.dart pins (a).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":368},"content_hash":"34304a7ffaa30c05614198cba34f952d747bec45f3b079a6b9d8cedf7566f14b"},"summary":"Android at medium (600-839) does not hold the toolbar: the home app keeps its own bar, search and New app beside a rail that also offers New app, Inbox and Settings","tags":["android","split","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.286255Z","id":"7e9c8f1f99d713afadfd5f5076825283cb1f70566acffb6706a6cfa9d208ce40","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.4 puts Search in the Mac toolbar, filtering the sidebar and, with Home selected, the grid. Toolbar.swift builds no NSSearchToolbarItem yet, so the filter (SidebarModel.filter) has its own field at the bottom of ClaxSidebar, which ⌘F focuses (SplitShell._showFilter); it narrows only the sidebar, not the grid.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":164},"content_hash":"32a2bc85addd41327b0d0d70efaa35b5d5217bf7b5671a51138cb4b6a11463f2"},"summary":"The sidebar's filter is a field at the sidebar's foot, not the toolbar's NSSearchToolbarItem","supersedes":"f1d30bf1dcaa1dd369dd223ba7dd7dcfabeebc1672f99cc99287ffaefc9d6cdd","tags":["macos","revisit:Toolbar.swift has an NSSearchToolbarItem","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
