{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.405096Z","id":"f2ef8d9a793742f100889c15e1894cbc91fc3ec49027aa4a450ca14f576ab8e8","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.4 has one Search item that filters the sidebar, and the grid when Home is selected, on ⌘F. The sidebar keeps its own filter field (lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart, 'sidebar-filter') because an app's toolbar (lib/ui/app_screen.dart _toolbarItems) declares no Search item yet, so ⌘F with an app selected has nowhere else to go; with Home selected the toolbar's field is the grid's search, and the sidebar filter stays one ⌘F away once an app is selected. split_shell_test 'Command-F puts the keyboard in the toolbar's search with Home selected…' pins this.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"a0b444a9de7d259de2cbb15f52238fc654086ef55fc1fe795857300292fe8a00"},"summary":"⌘F goes to the toolbar's search only with Home selected; with an app selected it still opens the sidebar's filter, and the toolbar's search filters the grid, not the sidebar","supersedes":"caf7f6c3cf2ef0c0d6a35773294a21ad7e24c53a8e65980a97b40b519c73c9eb","tags":["split","macos","revisit:when an app's toolbar declares the Search item of §4.4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.458969Z","id":"29c82092d0524e2e21babfab582771bc1e50afe773ddbf697b62f560861ff7e8","body":{"detail":"MainMenu.xib has no Delete App or starred-app items, so AppKit never routes these keys to Dart while the page is first responder. Adding File › Delete App… (⌘⌫) and Window items for the starred apps (⌘1…⌘9) through MacMenu would make them work from the page as the other commands do; whether those items belong in the menu bar (§4.8 lists neither) is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":605},"end":{"line":613},"content_hash":"6f2f6ac2fbf4c1f128c64c7a444abca5d64e5e4758084c572db463006b25a373"},"summary":"⌘⌫, ⌘1…⌘9 and Space reach the shell only while a Flutter view has the keyboard: with an app's page (its WKWebView) focused they go to the page, and no menu item carries them","supersedes":"05c0e170d282e0c5fca6a2d63c371d6f9f87b6198bc6229e5f602ed4eaf59851","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.520953Z","id":"4cb2a5d58d7e30de616500dc46cf32fdf87e1b991378866c45f9da89fd1a7f4d","body":{"detail":"In the split window the detail follows the selection (↑/↓ change both), so there is nothing further to open for an app. Moving focus into the detail is unverified with a page's WKWebView: Flutter's focus may land on the screen's first Flutter control rather than the page.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":354},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"515fc08575cf1e5f4df47d663ba0be3dd3a10cf92ffbc165f61927b58fe97a68"},"summary":"Space in the sidebar 'opens' the selected app by moving the keyboard into its detail (and a make's build view), since selecting a row already shows the app; a separate open state, or Space as Quick Look-style preview, was not taken","supersedes":"93f48ef646c17c1bc3c3f7d599020a0ae9402feeb507e0e19b95f8a1997435ad","tags":["revisit:when the detail can hold an app that is selected but not yet loaded, or the page must take the keyboard on Space","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.575929Z","id":"60a013b28bf59b822d9bf18d58b093a087e1a73214c3b8a99bd3cde399f3af14","body":{"detail":"SplitShellState._report holds HomeHost's toolbar for the Material family only at ClaxWidth.expanded, where ClaxListPane's search feeds HomeHost.setQuery. At medium no list pane shows, so holding would leave the grid without a search; not holding duplicates New app (and Inbox and Settings where the home app's bar has them). Options: (a) keep as is; (b) hold at medium too and put a search field above the grid in Flutter (or in the rail); (c) hold at medium and accept no search until Ctrl+F brings the list pane over the detail. Test: 'wide Android holds the toolbar…' in test/ui/split/split_shell_test.dart pins (a).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":430},"content_hash":"34304a7ffaa30c05614198cba34f952d747bec45f3b079a6b9d8cedf7566f14b"},"summary":"Android at medium (600-839) does not hold the toolbar: the home app keeps its own bar, search and New app beside a rail that also offers New app, Inbox and Settings","supersedes":"8d89d96004da2a15aedab1df15aad22068ea2e3ca380a987fa8b30f0f9c1e80e","tags":["android","split","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.611093Z","id":"89b803c6e3abc1f40c8c2febd0850e8945f4637e431464fd00cfbc400630ddaa","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:macos_app built, and the app ran from a scratch support directory (daemon on a free loopback port), but screencapture answered 'could not create image from window' for its window and for the display, so nothing was looked at. The renders of //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_split_shots_test draw stand-ins for the material, the window buttons and the toolbar.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"4f02b9919f81be8991f9ab21970e610cbb58af943a97b0b363e05708abb793b3"},"summary":"The split window is unverified in the running Mac app: the sidebar material through the clear view, the toolbar's toggle, the title and dragging the sidebar's edge","supersedes":"3a933ee7a968038c94fe95169ca38ca87eaf9cab5a173236af304b1d88554495","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.128571Z","id":"7b9a8cf0cb1e372b004215a5d166037b0b199920b18154775b403db7984f2f9e","body":{"detail":"SplitShell.hingeOf reads MediaQuery.displayFeaturesOf in window coordinates and takes the shell to start at x 0 (with the rail's 80 as start on Material), true while SplitShell is the app's home. apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox/inbox_split.dart keeps its 360 list at any hinge; spec §3.2 says the split between panes sits on the hinge, which covers the rail's Inbox too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"245e5e6eb82fc6c0cff60904ed5ddd312334e8e52eba49e0a128136527b035c5"},"suggested_fix":"Give InboxSplit the hinge through SplitShell.hingeOf with start ClaxLayout.rail when it is the rail's destination.","summary":"The hinge split assumes the split's panes start at the window's left edge, and the inbox's own list-detail beside the rail (InboxSplit) does not sit on the hinge","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.128862Z","id":"4f9bac3a42728282496b734c241b7045ddb8f15d2cffd0b958007b863e843500","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"245e5e6eb82fc6c0cff60904ed5ddd312334e8e52eba49e0a128136527b035c5"},"summary":"The hinge split, Control shortcuts, right-click menus and hover are tested only in widget tests: unverified on a real foldable (its hinge's display feature and posture) and on a Chromebook (its keyboard and mouse reaching Flutter)","tags":["phase:8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/list_pane.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.129664Z","id":"85ac18bbe00a39ccdfba7e39de3f4a1141cf31cab1d18dd4619d27f2824b686a","body":{"detail":"Spec §3.2 gives the rail New app, Home, Inbox and Settings and the list pane Search, Starred, Apps and Making, and names no place for Import app…, which the launcher's bar carried at phone and medium widths and the Mac's File menu carries. Other places: a rail destination under Settings, an item in New app's sheet, or a footer row of the list pane.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"93023de85f145641d4081c5d6da55196cbd2729023fbfd33287e29b273a26be1"},"summary":"Where Import app… lives beside wide Android's rail is a guess: the list pane's search bar has a More menu holding only it","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
